  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved socio-econcomic data, including youth labour market statistics, are collected and used in policy formulation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One key priority area of ILO work is the improvement of labour statistics. The ILO has provided training and support to enhance the capacity of local institutions including in particular the National Statistics Office (NSO) and labour/employment ministries to collect, analyze, and utilize labour market data effectively, in line with the latest standards adopted at the International Conference of Labour Statisticians (ICLS). For Vanuatu specifically, the ILO is providing technical and financial support to the first-ever Labour Force Survey conducted in Vanuatu, for which data collection will be completed in mid-2025. The LFS results are expected to be published by the NSO towards the end of 2025. The LFS includes a module to measure the impact of climate change and natural disasters on the Vanuatuan labour market, offering the possibility for learning and sharing of experiences between Pacific Island countries. This activity is supported by the SSTC Project on &quot;Improving labour market statistics to reflect climate impact on labour market outcomes in the Asia-Pacific region through South-South Cooperation&quot;.</narrative>
  </description>
